  "verification_scope": "Both reproductions inventoried, with targeted visual checking of marks, missing Q10(c), code, logic and tree figure. Not a symbol-by-symbol equivalence or original-completeness certification. No solutions authored or copied.",
  "discrepancies": [
    {
      "question": "10(c)",
      "note": "GFG page 7 includes converting the grammar from part (b) to remove left recursion, explicitly 4 marks. GateForum ends Q10 at (b) on page 10 and begins Q11 on page 11: this is confirmed missing content in that reproduction."
    },
    {
      "question": "3(xi)",
      "note": "GFG has five options A–E including C about monitors ensuring no deadlocks. GateForum omits that monitor option and shifts the later options; its first option also prints hashing instead of thrashing. Preserve source-specific option lettering."
    },
    {
      "question": "1(iv)",
      "note": "GateForum prints 8087 CPU; GFG prints 8086 CPU paired with the 8087 coprocessor. Treat this as a transcription variant."
    },
    {
      "question": "7",
      "note": "GateForum loses part of the instruction-format description; GFG pages 5–6 retain single-address CPU and 16-bit instruction length with lower 8 bits for operand address."
    },
    {
      "question": "9",
      "note": "Visual check confirms GateForum retains P(x,x*y,z), the initial assignments and the outer block of the scoping example. OCR alone falsely suggested missing code. No code-omission claim is made."
    },
    {
      "question": "10",
      "note": "GateForum renders the division-operator production as a visual fraction, which must not be mistaken for a missing production. GFG retains ordinary slash notation."
    },
    {
      "question": "12",
      "note": "Four labelled database query requests are separate leaves. Shared schema is on GateForum page 11 and individual requests on page 12; GFG has all on page 7."
    },
    {
      "question": "14",
      "note": "The binary-tree figure is present in both reproductions. It is not a missing-figure case. Root 1, children 5/18; 5 has 7/13, 18 has 25/20, 7 has 11/9, 13 has 15/17, 25 has left child 27."
    },
    {
      "question": "15(b)",
      "note": "GateForum raster retains negation in R(x,y) implies not R(y,x), despite faulty text extraction. Keep the full conjunction and multiple requested model properties together as one printed part."
    },
    {
      "question": "17(b)",
      "note": "GateForum prints a subscripted a1 where GFG specifies binary symbol 1. Do not silently treat that typography as a separate alphabet or new leaf."
    },
    {
      "question": "marks",
      "note": "Marks are sourced to the visibly printed GFG reproduction: A 74, B 126, sum 200. Q14 totals 6; other B groups total 10. Nested requests in 8(a), 9(a)/(b), and 12(a)/(b) share parent marks, so leaf marks remain null rather than divided arbitrarily. No optional-selection or negative-marking rule established."
    },
    {
      "question": "scope",
      "note": "All observed original groups 1–17 are inventoried, but this does not certify original completeness. Both are secondary reproductions; no official original or official answer key verified."
    }
  ],
